// i18n-obs-es — the es strings of the Trends, Projection and Observatory
// modes. One file per locale, injected by CveModes (js/cve-modes.js) only
// when the page is in this language and a dashboard mode is being prepared,
// so neither the List page nor a reader in another language pays for them;
// English needs no file at all. Same convention as i18n.js: English source
// strings ARE the keys, a missing entry falls back to English, and
// js/i18n-parity.test.mjs is what notices one. The eager mode-switch keys
// (Mode, List, Trends, Projection, Observatory, the loading note) live in
// i18n.js, because they show before any of these files arrives.
//
// I18N is a top-level const in the classic script i18n.js, so it is visible
// here; this file only extends it. Keep the %1…%n placeholders, in an order
// that reads naturally in the locale.
//
// Terminology, held the same across every panel:
//   - KEV, EPSS, CVSS, CWE, CPE, CNA and NVD stay in English (see i18n.js);
//     so do NVD's vulnStatus values (Received, Deferred…) where they are
//     quoted as fields, and the stats.json field names.
//   - "settled" / "still settling" (CONTRACT §13): consolidado / en
//     consolidación; consolidado / em consolidação; 確定 / 確定待ち;
//     устоялось / ещё уточняется.
//   - "projection" is never "forecast" in any language: proyección, projeção,
//     推計, проекция — not pronóstico, previsão, 予測 or прогноз. A
//     projection is arithmetic, not a call.
//   - "attested" (taken on the publisher's word) / "recomputable": declarado
//     / recalculable; 申告値 / 再計算可能; со слов издателя / пересчитываемо.
//   - "band" in a projection is a range of past errors: banda, faixa, 範囲,
//     интервал. A severity band is the CVSS band: banda, faixa, 帯, диапазон.

